# track/standback-2026-08-15 scope manifest
#
# MULTI-TRACK PROTOCOL rule 2: a track is a branch plus this file. Every path a
# commit on track/standback-2026-08-15 touches must match one of the globs
# below, and scripts/qa/locked_paths_gate.mjs fails CI otherwise.
#
# Declared 2026-08-15 by FS_REPORT_REVERT_2026-08-15_Prompt.md TASK 4, AFTER the
# work rather than before it, which rule 2 asks for the other way round. That is
# recorded rather than smoothed over: the stand-back session opened a track/
# branch without one, the gate caught it on run 31815432853, and this file is the
# repair. The scope below is therefore the EXACT set of paths the branch has
# actually touched, enumerated from git diff --name-only 90f21280..HEAD plus the
# files this repair adds. It is not widened by a single glob beyond that.
#
# Glob forms: an exact path; a trailing slash for a whole directory; ** for any
# depth and * for one segment.
#
# The locked paths are NOT excluded here and do not need to be. The same gate
# carries the locked-path rule separately, so a locked file still fails without
# an owner-sanction token even if a glob here matched it. None does.
#
# EXTENDED 2026-08-15 by FS_RED_CLEARANCE_2026-08-15_Prompt.md. The two dead
# manifests are MOVED, not deleted, so the branch touches both their old paths
# and docs/records/tracks/closed/. The disjoint check reads this directory
# non-recursively, so a manifest under closed/ is a record rather than a claim,
# and the check now reports 2 manifests, 0 collisions, 0 shared globs.
#
# SUPERSEDED 2026-08-15 by the move above, and kept as the record of why the move
# was needed. Everything below described the state between the two passes.
#
# MEASURED CONSEQUENCE, RECORDED HERE BECAUSE IT IS NOT OPTIONAL AND IS NOT OURS
# TO DECIDE. Committing this file clears the TRACK SCOPE failure and opens a
# DISJOINT failure in the same gate, run 2026-08-15:
#
#   DISJOINT: 4 manifest(s), 4466 tracked file(s), 14 file collision(s),
#   2 shared glob(s)
#
# All 14 collisions and both shared globs are against manifests whose BRANCHES NO
# LONGER EXIST. quality-sweep declares frontend/src/**, frontend/scripts/** and
# docs/QUALITY_CHARTER.md; docs-reskin declares COMPLIANCE_WATCH.md; both
# branches were deleted on 2026-07-28 and the verification is recorded at
# docs/records/BRANCH_HYGIENE_2026-07-28.md. The gate compares every .manifest
# file in this directory and has no way to know a track has finished.
#
# So no honest manifest for any new track that touches frontend/src can be
# disjoint while those two files remain. Narrowing THIS one to dodge the
# collision would make the scope check fail instead, because the branch really
# does touch those paths, and would be a manifest that lies.
#
# THE FIX IS ONE COMMAND AND IT IS NOT TAKEN HERE, because deleting another
# track's record sits outside this brief's staged paths and outside a builder's
# call: git rm docs/records/tracks/quality-sweep.manifest
# docs/records/tracks/docs-reskin.manifest. It waits for the owner's word.

